{"t": 1794119210.3863795, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "[FIRING] PaymentGatewayErrors checkout (OnCall AG-7731) - root cause identified\n\nGateway 4xx rate 38% since 07:41 UTC. Loki app=\"checkout\" shows the gateway rejecting charges with HTTP 400 invalid_amount: \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\". A log line at 07:41:05 says the gateway API version switched to 2026-11 (strict amounts), which now enforces integer minor units.\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py charge_payload() now converts EUR to integer cents before sending (12.34 EUR -> amount=1234, currency=EUR), using Decimal half-up rounding to avoid float drift.\n\nStatus: code fixed and verified locally; needs deploy to prod-eu-1 to stop the 4xxs. No other gateway fields appear in the error, but if 4xxs persist after deploy, check the next error body in Loki."}, "ok": true}
